  first input is [3, 1, 2], while the second [1, 3, 4] (as the axis is 1).
  >>> x = tf.constant([[3, 1, 2], [1, 3, 4]], dtype=tf.float32)
  >>> y, segments = tf.nn.isotonic_regression(x, axis=1)
  >>> y  # The solution.
  <tf.Tensor: shape=(2, 3), dtype=float32, numpy=
  array([[3.       , 1.5      , 1.5      ],
